  "exhibits": [
    {
      "id": "tcp-m2-tbs3-ex1",
      "title": "Shareholder items",
      "html": "<p>A direct loan with face amount $50,000 and tax basis $20,000 is fully repaid. Separately, another shareholder has stock basis $12,000, qualifying debt basis $8,000, and a $27,000 loss; ignore other limits.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "tcp-m2-tbs3-ex2",
      "title": "Entity tax",
      "html": "<p>The case determines a taxable built-in-gain base of $60,000 after all applicable limitations. Use a 21% tax rate.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "<h3>Gain on the full loan repayment</h3><p>$50,000 repayment less $20,000 basis = $30,000.</p><h3>Loss capacity from stock and debt basis</h3><p>$12,000 + $8,000 = $20,000.</p><h3>Loss suspended for lack of basis</h3><p>$27,000 − $20,000 = $7,000.</p><h3>Built-in-gains tax under supplied assumptions</h3><p>$60,000 × 21% = $12,600.</p>"
